&#x1F449;&#xA0;Interested in joining us? Apply today!","time":"2w","title":"National Latina Institute for Reproductive Justice"},{"date":"2025-11-26T20:31:58.943Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E22AQF3FyNU-vnkmA/feedshare-shrink_2048_1536/B4EZqjg5dwIQA0-/0/1763679902100?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=WhTE5K4Z6lOawLZ9kOYVBDrJTmKlADVqKSQQfEPZkHA"],"likes_count":2,"post_id":"7397419733127688192","post_url":"https://es.linkedin.com/posts/latinainstitute_la-carga-p%C3%BAblica-es-una-regla-propuesta-activity-7397419733127688192-TQ9s","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"La carga pública es una regla propuesta que dificultará a ciertos inmigrantes obtener la tarjeta de residencia si han recibido CUALQUIER tipo de ayuda del gobierno, lo que podría incluir Medicaid, ayuda alimentaria, ayuda para la vivienda y más. Nuestra directora ejecutiva @lupemrodriguez explica cómo esta propuesta amenaza la salud y la estabilidad económica de las comunidades inmigrantes. Pero la lucha no ha terminado. Hasta el 19 de diciembre, el Departamento de Seguridad Nacional está aceptando comentarios del público, que luego revisará antes de finalizar la propuesta.Es hora de que nos hagamos oír y exijamos que esta regla no se apruebe, que nuestras comunidades inmigrantes nunca tengan que elegir entre la comida, la vivienda y la atención médica, y la residencia. ¡Dirígete al enlace https://lnkd.in/etaC_w2t para enviar tu comentario y ayúdanos a detener este ataque racista y xenófobo contra nuestras comunidades!","text_html":"La carga p&#xFA;blica es una regla propuesta&#xA0; que dificultar&#xE1; a ciertos inmigrantes obtener la tarjeta de residencia si han recibido CUALQUIER tipo de ayuda del gobierno, lo que podr&#xED;a incluir Medicaid, ayuda alimentaria, ayuda para la vivienda y m&#xE1;s. Nuestra directora ejecutiva @lupemrodriguez explica c&#xF3;mo esta propuesta amenaza la salud y la estabilidad econ&#xF3;mica de las comunidades&#xA0;inmigrantes.

Pero la lucha no ha terminado. Hasta el 19 de diciembre, el Departamento de Seguridad Nacional est&#xE1; aceptando comentarios del p&#xFA;blico, que luego revisar&#xE1; antes de finalizar la <a class="link" href="http://propuesta.Es?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>propuesta.Es</a> hora de que nos hagamos o&#xED;r y exijamos que esta regla no se apruebe, que nuestras comunidades&#xA0; inmigrantes nunca tengan que elegir entre la comida, la vivienda y la atenci&#xF3;n m&#xE9;dica, y la residencia. &#xA1;Dir&#xED;gete al enlace <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/etaC_w2t?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/etaC_w2t</a> para enviar tu comentario y ay&#xFA;danos a detener este ataque racista y xen&#xF3;fobo contra nuestras comunidades!&#xA0; ","time":"2w","title":"National Latina Institute for Reproductive Justice"},{"comments_count":1,"date":"2025-11-26T20:31:58.958Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E22AQHxvXMNDIOZbw/feedshare-shrink_2048_1536/B4EZqjgh1JHoAw-/0/1763679805189?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=8fEB81rN8C_P91Of8X-nUZ1h11kHccESCkekwSd8Zm0"],"likes_count":21,"post_id":"7397409266195902464","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/latinainstitute_public-charge-is-a-harmful-proposed-rule-activity-7397409266195902464-JDPK","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"Public Charge is a harmful proposed rule that would make it harder for certain immigrants to obtain a green card if they’ve received ANY government assistance– – that might include Medicaid, food assistance, housing assistance, and more. Executive Director Lupe M. R. explains how this proposal threatens the health and economic stability of immigrant communities. But the fight isn’t over. Until December 19th, the Department of Homeland Security is accepting comments from the public, which it will then review before making a final decision. It’s time we get LOUD and demand this rule not be made final, that our immigrant communities never have to choose between food, housing, and medical care, and green card status. Head to https://lnkd.in/etaC_w2t to submit your comment and help us stop this racist, xenophobic attack on our communities!","text_html":"Public Charge is a harmful proposed rule that would make it harder for certain immigrants to obtain a green card if they&#x2019;ve received ANY government assistance&#x2013; &#x2013; that might include Medicaid, food assistance, housing assistance, and more. Executive Director <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lupe-m-rodr%C3%ADguez?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Lupe M. R.</a> explains how this proposal threatens the health and economic stability of immigrant communities.

But the fight isn&#x2019;t over. Until December 19th, the Department of Homeland Security is accepting comments from the public, which it will then review before making a final decision. It&#x2019;s time we get LOUD and demand this rule not be made final, that our immigrant communities never have to choose between food, housing, and medical care, and green card status. Head to <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/etaC_w2t?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/etaC_w2t</a> to submit your comment and help us stop this racist, xenophobic attack on our communities!","time":"2w Edited","title":"National Latina Institute for Reproductive Justice"},{"date":"2025-11-19T20:31:58.960Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E22AQGk5zWX6tTpug/feedshare-shrink_1280/B4EZqTtEh8KoAs-/0/1763414658607?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=xtYNlOpPpno5vImqO2Ca0g5FxBMkfEvzHZc0x94Zycs","https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E22AQFSxFZsbPqYdQ/feedshare-shrink_1280/B4EZqTtEgvIoAs-/0/1763414658261?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=nVZ1IF9W3_zHZjIjFvXtOpbQE_RNSRbiQPAWWdtQ1ik","https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E22AQGT3JW-ipN8fg/feedshare-shrink_1280/B4EZqTtEhIJgA0-/0/1763414658106?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=mmXvjIYd-dJxIWHULLVV4hI7u6nEEryEOY7f-7eYr7w","https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E22AQHvmZYqESTUnQ/feedshare-shrink_2048_1536/B4EZqTtEhGKsA4-/0/1763414658634?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=Xi_7qFdE2K4_bconZ39wn9QBiMHBKH49_Mh_s9wo72c","https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E22AQH8i1FtTNqlug/feedshare-shrink_2048_1536/B4EZqTtEhVHMA0-/0/1763414658714?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=Hs5yBBK7QBlHXm_smtRXY9CgOLtNEqkNydVCWUJLl9M"],"likes_count":6,"post_id":"7396551526846205953","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/latinainstitute_check-it-out-its-another-media-roundup-activity-7396551526846205953-5OD_","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"📣 Check it out! It’s another Media Roundup! 📣 We’re highlighting the incredible op-eds from our fellows participating in the Op-Ed Project! They’re discussing topics ranging from the problem of pain in reproductive care to the intersection of abortion bans and anti-trans legislation to the threat of denaturalization faced by our immigrant communities to the state of U.S. reproductive care access three years after Roe to how pregnant bodies are policed. All in all: they’re tackling important topics and bringing critical perspective to these conversations! 🤩 Check out the highlights!","text_html":"&#x1F4E3; Check it out! It&#x2019;s another Media Roundup! &#x1F4E3;

We&#x2019;re highlighting the incredible op-eds from our fellows participating in the Op-Ed Project! They&#x2019;re discussing topics ranging from the problem of pain in reproductive care to the intersection of abortion bans and anti-trans legislation to the threat of denaturalization faced by our immigrant communities to the state of U.S. reproductive care access three years after Roe to how pregnant bodies are policed. All in all: they&#x2019;re tackling important topics and bringing critical perspective to these conversations! &#x1F929;

