Contains AI-generated elements.","time":"1w","title":"Liebherr Aerospace and Transportation","videos":["https://dms.licdn.com/playlist/vid/v2/D4D10AQG2hlpeAWxVvQ/mp4-360p-30fp-crf28/B4DZtVRgQ9H0B0-/0/1766662217023?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=smWHpUG-DoOde0zvKrvYxjO9I2pWwIZuXXpGeCwBzYM","https://dms.licdn.com/playlist/vid/v2/D4D10AQG2hlpeAWxVvQ/mp4-720p-30fp-crf28/B4DZtVRgQ9H0B4-/0/1766662217023?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=2miELB_Sze5yOPzoh8MeDx-gqCc556jEDAZ2cQ4pKXc","https://dms.licdn.com/playlist/vid/v2/D4D10AQG2hlpeAWxVvQ/mp4-640p-30fp-crf28/B4DZtVRgQ9H0BY-/0/1766662217024?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=9VL235I7BCXWA4XuSROHn7IX6gZKSlcaSYP4OnCcoS4"]},{"comments_count":2,"date":"2025-12-19T09:36:54.287Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4D10AQESGq_1DixVFw/image-shrink_800/B4DZs11myHKwAk-/0/1766134804113?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=Q3MHkYbamhmgFeRHuK4jSB6E28KOehFvGC7HQAVPFuc"],"likes_count":92,"post_id":"7407706415517130752","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/liebherr-aerospace-and-transportation_liebherr-solutionprovider-additivemanufacturing-activity-7407706415517130752--ggx","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"Layer by layer: 2025 was a very busy year for our additive manufacturing departments. Here's a quick recap! 🙌 ➡️ Additive Manufacturing – AM for short, also known as 3D printing – holds significant promise and plays an important role in both current and future aircraft. This year was another busy one for us, with printers running at full speed at our sites in Toulouse (France) and Lindenberg (Germany): 🖨️ The aluminum alloy printer in Toulouse clocked 2,000 to 3,000 hours of printing time. 🖨️ The non metallic powder printers in Lindenberg ran for almost 3,000 hours and the titanium powder printer for around 3,500 hours. We have a vast collection of components that are manufactured in series using additive manufacturing processes: for example sensor brackets for landing gears, lower cargo door actuator manifolds as well as valve components and heat exchangers. ✈️ Impressive, isn't it? #liebherr #solutionprovider #additivemanufacturing #alm #3d","text_html":"Layer by layer: 2025 was a very busy year for our additive manufacturing departments. Here&apos;s a quick recap! &#x1F64C;

&#x27A1;&#xFE0F; Additive Manufacturing &#x2013; AM for short, also known as 3D printing &#x2013; holds significant promise and plays an important role in both current and future aircraft. This year was another busy one for us, with printers running at full speed at our sites in Toulouse (France) and Lindenberg (Germany):

&#x1F5A8;&#xFE0F; The aluminum alloy printer in Toulouse clocked 2,000 to 3,000 hours of printing time. 

&#x1F5A8;&#xFE0F; The non metallic powder printers in Lindenberg ran for almost 3,000 hours and the titanium powder printer for around 3,500 hours. 

We have a vast collection of components that are manufactured in series using additive manufacturing processes: for example sensor brackets for landing gears, lower cargo door actuator manifolds as well as valve components and heat exchangers. &#x2708;&#xFE0F;

Impressive, isn&apos;t it?   

<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fliebherr&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#liebherr</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fsolutionprovider&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#solutionprovider</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fadditivemanufacturing&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#additivemanufacturing</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Falm&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#alm</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2F3d&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#3d</a> ","time":"2w","title":"Liebherr Aerospace and Transportation"},{"date":"2025-12-19T09:36:54.290Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E10AQEJ38EdUFXFeg/image-shrink_1280/B4EZsr946BIQAc-/0/1765969203300?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=4qqme5gu3-tm32q5GILL8QAC9FBOfA7HPv7YLtX4zsU"],"likes_count":87,"post_id":"7407011822307917824","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/liebherr-aerospace-and-transportation_liebherr-solutionprovider-aircraft-activity-7407011822307917824-6Pr0","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"Keeping the right balance ⚖️ ➡️ Compressors and turbine wheels are key parts of the turbomachinery used in aircraft air-conditioning systems. They enable the compression and expansion stages of the air cycle cooling process. Rotating at very high speeds - ranging from 30.000 to 85.000 rpm depending on the application - they require very high precision machining and balancing. ✈️ #liebherr #solutionprovider #aircraft #airconditioning","text_html":"Keeping the right balance &#x2696;&#xFE0F;

&#x27A1;&#xFE0F; Compressors and turbine wheels are key parts of the turbomachinery used in aircraft air-conditioning systems. They enable the compression and expansion stages of the air cycle cooling process. 

Rotating at very high speeds - ranging from 30.000 to 85.000 rpm depending on the application - they require very high precision machining and balancing. &#x2708;&#xFE0F;

<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fliebherr&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#liebherr</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fsolutionprovider&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#solutionprovider</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Faircraft&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#aircraft</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fairconditioning&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#airconditioning</a>  ","time":"2w","title":"Liebherr Aerospace and Transportation"},{"comments_count":1,"date":"2025-12-19T09:36:54.305Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4D10AQFsAIsSvwlNcg/image-shrink_800/B4DZsSbrK4IgAg-/0/1765540803662?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=egy1RfAKd7BpMxObENFUsJ313SVRcGuR58a1RnkOMto","https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4D10AQFeNrXPSaW4Bg/image-shrink_800/B4DZsSbrIhLUAg-/0/1765540803528?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=IujlnHpxzDvwcknCtRajXomLTKo6XzFNiYqLFjetsRw"],"likes_count":135,"post_id":"7405215045317545984","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/liebherr-aerospace-and-transportation_liebherr-liebherraerospace-aerospace-activity-7405215045317545984--XnZ","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"The Aviation Forum in December is one of the highlights at the end of the year - once again in beautiful Hamburg (Germany). 🌊 The challenges and opportunities in the aerospace industry are ongoing, and the Aviation Forum is a key event to exchange ideas. Two of our Managing Directors from our Liebherr-Aerospace site in Lindenberg (Germany) took part in the stage program and shared their views: ➡️ Gerd Heinzelmann contributed to a panel discussion on “How Aero Excellence is driving supplier maturity and performance during this crucial phase of global ramp-up” together with Pierre Perdoux , TORRES Hugo , and Jörg Schuler . ➡️ Additionally, Philipp Walter participated in the closing and outlook session, “Towards 2030: Building a resilient, transparent, and future-ready aerospace supply chain,” and had an engaging exchange with Nils Witt , Lejla N. , Yves Yemsi , and Stefan BDLI-Berndes. Thank you to everyone for the inspiring conversations both on and off stage. This is what moves us forward! 💪 #liebherr #liebherraerospace #aerospace #aviationforum #afo25","text_html":"The <a class="link" href="https://de.linkedin.com/showcase/aviation-forum-2026/?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Aviation Forum</a> in December is one of the highlights at the end of the year - once again in beautiful Hamburg (Germany). &#x1F30A;

The challenges and opportunities in the aerospace industry are ongoing, and the Aviation Forum is a key event to exchange ideas. 

Two of our Managing Directors from our Liebherr-Aerospace site in Lindenberg (Germany) took part in the stage program and shared their views: 

&#x27A1;&#xFE0F; <a class="link" href="https://de.linkedin.com/in/gerd-heinzelmann-2b161b23b?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Gerd Heinzelmann</a> contributed to a panel discussion on &#x201C;How Aero Excellence is driving supplier maturity and performance during this crucial phase of global ramp-up&#x201D; together with <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/in/pierre-perdoux-62524515?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Pierre Perdoux</a>, <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/in/torres-hugo-86977520?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>TORRES Hugo</a>, and <a class="link" href="https://de.linkedin.com/in/j%C3%B6rg-schuler-a9aa33b1?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>J&#xF6;rg Schuler</a>.

&#x27A1;&#xFE0F; Additionally, Philipp Walter participated in the closing and outlook session, &#x201C;Towards 2030: Building a resilient, transparent, and future-ready aerospace supply chain,&#x201D; and had an engaging exchange with <a class="link" href="https://de.linkedin.com/in/nils-witt-4b822519a?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Nils Witt</a>, <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lejla-n-72b6678?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Lejla N.</a>, <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/in/yvesyemsi?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Yves Yemsi</a>, and Stefan BDLI-Berndes.

Thank you to everyone for the inspiring conversations both on and off stage. This is what moves us forward! &#x1F4AA;

