On November 18, we, along with EBRD , hosted our ninth workshop focused on Resolution Planning and MREL topics, under the theme "above and beyond." 🙌 We looked at new #regulatory development in the Resolution and Recovery frame works with esteemed guests from Single Resolution Board, Austrian, Romanian, Bosnian and Croatian resolution authorities. 🤗 EBRD, IFC, and OPEC fund, along with CEE DCM experts from BNP, shared investment opportunities and market developments. We went beyond traditional MREL requirements, exploring how Significant Risk Transfer instruments can optimize bank balance sheets, examining benefits, threats, and perspectives from rating agencies, investors, and regulators. #MakeItHappen","text_html":"<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fmrel&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#MREL</a> Above and Beyond &#x1F91D;

What started nine years ago as a small working group under the Vienna Initiative has grown into a key gathering of experts from resolution authorities, supranational institutions, banks, rating agencies, and regulators. On November 18, we, along with <a class="link" href="https://uk.linkedin.com/company/ebrd?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>EBRD</a>, hosted our ninth workshop focused on Resolution Planning and MREL topics, under the theme &quot;above and beyond.&quot; &#x1F64C;

We looked at new <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fregulatory&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#regulatory</a> development in the Resolution and Recovery frame works with esteemed guests from&#xA0;Single Resolution Board, Austrian, Romanian, Bosnian and Croatian resolution authorities.&#xA0;&#x1F917;

EBRD, IFC, and OPEC fund, along with CEE DCM experts from BNP, shared investment opportunities and market developments. We went beyond traditional MREL requirements, exploring how Significant Risk Transfer instruments can optimize bank balance sheets, examining benefits, threats, and perspectives from rating agencies, investors, and regulators. 

