[{"comments_count":2,"date":"2026-01-02T13:57:50.915Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E10AQH57FlxZ-5R-w/image-shrink_800/B4EZt9gp1rJQAg-/0/1767337271109?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=yIET8fgPQbjfoNdR_61gpUPZ_UmWlIcNVoDryveflOc","https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E10AQE-qJLks01S4g/image-shrink_800/B4EZt9gqY9KUAg-/0/1767337273421?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=5uryeNQqZgBfcRS4bUACxPCLAmz8AOHt7jTwgQmQj8E","https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E10AQGMxTKVsJQ64w/image-shrink_800/B4EZt9grJyHoAg-/0/1767337276570?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=Cne-1aOGTdfs2pNKaVlvLeRmu5E6U8ngA6wTujoY9v4","https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E10AQHPhhjcLR1h4g/image-shrink_800/B4EZt9gr0tGcAg-/0/1767337279229?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=Bo7hbcdUPPFokesezUits7R1jTJe44NlmTtOIlTdbgk","https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E10AQE4CaZ5j5jEUQ/image-shrink_800/B4EZt9gsVEKkAg-/0/1767337281494?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=phcfyq6TJwGidgUncoH_iZgV8eBWXY0mfwgZgwLWWEM"],"likes_count":84,"post_id":"7412749843816660992","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/daimlertruckag_unimog-ux100-daimlertruck-activity-7412749843816660992-IJPt","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"The best things come in small packages: the Mercedes-Benz Unimog 409 series. 🫶🚚 Let's go back in time: in 1996, an out of the ordinary #Unimog celebrated its debut - the 409 series. The “Mini Unimog” was designed as a small implement carrier for use by local municipalities. With a width of just 1.6 m and a total height of less than 2 m, it could also be used down narrow streets or in places requiring a particularly high level of manoeuvrability. At the same time, the implement carrier launched as the #UX100 had a lot of the technology and equipment features of its big brother on board . In addition to the all-wheel drive, this includes the practical interfaces for attachments and accessories. The UX 100 was launched in two variants. With a wheelbase of only 2,150 mm, the UX 100 H could be used as a compact implement carrier, while the UX 100 M with a wheelbase of 2,600 mm was primarily designed for transport tasks. However, after just a few years, Daimler parted with the UX 100, which was continued at Hako under the name "Kommobil”. Did you like this brief history lesson? Let us know in the comments! ✍️ #DaimlerTruck #Throwback","text_html":"The best things come in small packages: the <a class="link" href="https://de.linkedin.com/company/mercedes-benz-unimog?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Mercedes-Benz Unimog</a> 409 series. &#x1FAF6;&#x1F69A;

Let&apos;s go back in time: in 1996, an out of the ordinary <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Funimog&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#Unimog</a> celebrated its debut - the 409 series. The &#x201C;Mini Unimog&#x201D; was designed as a small implement carrier for use by local municipalities.

With a width of just 1.6 m and a total height of less than 2 m, it could also be used down narrow streets or in places requiring a particularly high level of manoeuvrability. At the same time, the implement carrier launched as the <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fux100&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#UX100</a> had a lot of the technology and equipment features of its big brother on board . In addition to the all-wheel drive, this includes the practical interfaces for attachments and accessories.

The UX 100 was launched in two variants. With a wheelbase of only 2,150 mm, the UX 100 H could be used as a compact implement carrier, while the UX 100 M with a wheelbase of 2,600 mm was primarily designed for transport tasks. However, after just a few years, Daimler parted with the UX 100, which was continued at Hako under the name &quot;Kommobil&#x201D;.

Did you like this brief history lesson? Let us know in the comments! &#x270D;&#xFE0F;

