Thank you to everyone for coming together to support your community and spread some Christmas joy this year!&#xA0;","time":"3w","title":"Services Australia"},{"comments_count":2,"date":"2025-12-12T13:57:12.269Z","likes_count":39,"post_id":"7403586211128238080","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/services-australia_applications-for-our-semester-and-trimester-activity-7403586211128238080-G_Nq","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"Applications for our semester and trimester 1 2026 university student placements are now open! During the placement, you’ll get a chance to develop your skills while working on a variety of tasks. You’ll gain a greater understanding of our agency and the public service. When you complete a placement with us, you’ll get: ★ valuable insights into how the public sector works and see how we deliver vital services to Australians ★ real workplace experience and the opportunity to apply skills from your university studies ★ to work in one of our many offices, service centres or smart centres across Australia. University student placements are unpaid and count towards academic credits. Applications close 2 January 2026. For more information about the placements, go to the link in our comments.","text_html":"Applications for our semester and trimester 1 2026 university student placements are now open! 

During the placement, you&#x2019;ll get a chance to develop your skills while working on a variety of tasks. You&#x2019;ll gain a greater understanding of our agency and the public service. 

When you complete a placement with us, you&#x2019;ll get:&#xA0;
&#x2605; valuable insights into how the public sector works and see how we deliver vital services to Australians&#xA0;
&#x2605; real workplace experience and the opportunity to apply skills from your university studies&#xA0;
&#x2605; to work in one of our many offices, service centres or smart centres across Australia. 

University student placements are unpaid and count towards academic credits. 

Applications close 2 January 2026. For more information about the placements, go to the link in our comments.&#xA0;","time":"3w","title":"Services Australia"}]

[{"comments_count":1,"date":"2025-12-04T20:25:26.602Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D5622AQGGjohwoQMzag/feedshare-shrink_2048_1536/B56Zrmfu9nLsAw-/0/1764803670383?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=BkA9yUataazagSECUN3SLkULHfUqGtvL225NzvY2oY0"],"likes_count":8,"post_id":"7402123100043288576","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/oregon-department-of-justice_its-the-time-of-year-where-many-oregonians-activity-7402123100043288576-EfHu","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"It’s the time of year where many Oregonians make charitable contributions. If you plan to give to any charities this year, here are six tips to make sure your donations have the biggest impact: — 1. Be proactive. Decide what causes are most important to you, and what difference you want your dollars to make in your community. Avoid responding to solicitations from unfamiliar organizations. Instead, reach out directly to the charities you want to support. — 2. Do your research. Did you know there are more than 1 million charities registered with the IRS? These websites can help you find charities with missions and programs you may like to support: https://give.org https://lnkd.in/ebNumQf https://candid.org — 3. Only give to registered charities. Before you give, check the Oregon DOJ charity database at https://lnkd.in/gAhEHZAc or call 971-673-1880 to confirm the organization is properly registered. Our database has copies of required financial reports, so you can learn about how charities spend donations. — 4. Be wary of text, email, telephone or door-to-door solicitations. Clicking on links in unsolicited email or texts can lead to a scammer’s website. Many charity scams pull on your heartstrings or use high pressure to convince you to give. Resist these tactics. In addition, don’t respond to solicitations that ask you to pay via a gift card or wire transfer. When you are ready to give, go directly to the charity’s website to find the best way to contribute. — 5. If you donate through a fundraising platform, read the fine print. Fundraising platforms often make donating easier - but they may charge fees or add on a “tip” to support the platform. Some platforms may not immediately transfer your donation to your selected charity. Before making your donation through an online platform, look for information about how your donation will be processed. Make sure there are no unanticipated fees or tips that have been added to your donation at checkout. — 6. Remember that not all gifts are tax-deductible. Only gifts to charities that have IRS 501(c)(3) status are tax-deductible. If taking a deduction is important to you, use the IRS search tool to check on the organization’s status: https://lnkd.in/gYQhbsPh Make sure the charity provides written confirmation of your donation. Then keep your records. Gifts to individuals through GoFundMe and similar websites are not tax-deductible. — If you have concerns about a charity or solicitation, please file a complaint online at https://lnkd.in/gCsrg33j or call the Charitable Activities Section at 971-673-1880. Thank you for your generosity and engaging in Wise Giving!","text_html":"It&#x2019;s the time of year where many Oregonians make charitable contributions. 

If you plan to give to any charities this year, here are six tips to make sure your donations have the biggest impact:&#xA0;
&#xA0;
&#x2014;

1. Be proactive.

Decide what causes are most important to you, and what difference you want your dollars to make in your community. Avoid responding to solicitations from unfamiliar organizations. Instead, reach out directly to the charities you want to support.

&#x2014;
&#xA0;
2. Do your research.

Did you know there are more than 1 million charities registered with the IRS? These websites can help you find charities with missions and programs you may like to support:
<a class="link" href="https://give.org?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://give.org</a>
<a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/ebNumQf?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/ebNumQf</a>
<a class="link" href="https://candid.org?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://candid.org</a>

&#x2014;
&#xA0;
3. Only give to registered charities.

Before you give, check the Oregon DOJ charity database at <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gAhEHZAc?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gAhEHZAc</a> or call 971-673-1880 to confirm the organization is properly registered. Our database has copies of required financial reports, so you can learn about how charities spend donations.

&#x2014;
&#xA0;
4. Be wary of text, email, telephone or door-to-door solicitations.

Clicking on links in unsolicited email or texts can lead to a scammer&#x2019;s website. Many charity scams pull on your heartstrings or use high pressure to convince you to give. Resist these tactics. In addition, don&#x2019;t respond to solicitations that ask you to pay via a gift card or wire transfer. When you are ready to give, go directly to the charity&#x2019;s website to find the best way to contribute.

&#x2014;
&#xA0;
5. If you donate through a fundraising platform, read the fine print.

Fundraising platforms often make donating easier - but they may charge fees or add on a &#x201C;tip&#x201D; to support the platform. Some platforms may not immediately transfer your donation to your selected charity. Before making your donation through an online platform, look for information about how your donation will be processed. Make sure there are no unanticipated fees or tips that have been added to your donation at checkout.
&#xA0;
&#x2014;

6. Remember that not all gifts are tax-deductible.

Only gifts to charities that have IRS 501(c)(3) status are tax-deductible. If taking a deduction is important to you, use the IRS search tool to check on the organization&#x2019;s status: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gYQhbsPh?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gYQhbsPh</a>
Make sure the charity provides written confirmation of your donation. Then keep your records. Gifts to individuals through GoFundMe and similar websites are not tax-deductible.
&#xA0;
&#x2014;

If you have concerns about a charity or solicitation, please file a complaint online at <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gCsrg33j?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gCsrg33j</a> or call the Charitable Activities Section at 971-673-1880.
&#xA0;
