Learn more and apply at <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gQd_JXJt?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gQd_JXJt</a>.","time":"2w","title":"Oregon Department of Justice"},{"comments_count":2,"date":"2025-10-11T20:25:26.610Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D5622AQE8JbEPvohwMw/feedshare-shrink_800/B56ZnEue.XJkAk-/0/1759942144561?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=AcPKOXVEWxGfBcnnZMrRAbxxyzxDcr1-O25hY5-B00A"],"likes_count":51,"post_id":"7382082471192006656","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/oregon-department-of-justice_we-recently-convened-a-roundtable-with-six-activity-7382082471192006656-XTdl","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"We recently convened a roundtable with six attorneys general and national leaders to discuss how state AGs are working together to combat the challenges facing consumers and workers. In states across the country, AGs are stepping in where federal enforcement has been rolled back — including the weakening of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau and the Federal Trade Commission — and focusing resources on the issues that matter most to working families. Here at the Oregon DOJ, we’re committed to fighting for working families every day. This roundtable was the first step in expanding our knowledge of best practices and increasing collaboration with others. Joining us were AG Nick Brown (Washington), AG Keith Ellison (Minnesota), AG Kwame Raoul (Illinois), AG Brian Schwalb (Washington DC), and AG Matthew Platkin (New Jersey). We were also joined by prominent labor and workforce leaders, including Graham Trainor (Oregon AFL-CIO), Terri Gerstein (NYU Wagner Labor Initiative), Josh Diamond (Leadership Center for Attorney General Studies), Samuel Levine (UC Berkeley Center for Consumer Law and Economic Justice; former Director of the FTC Bureau of Consumer Protection), Seth Frotman (UC Berkeley Center for Consumer Law and Economic Justice; former CFPB General Counsel and Senior Advisor to the Director), Erin Witte (Consumer Federation of America), and Shelmun Dashan (UC Berkeley Center for Consumer Law and Economic Justice).","text_html":"We recently convened a roundtable with six attorneys general and national leaders to discuss how state AGs are working together to combat the challenges facing consumers and workers. 

In states across the country, AGs are stepping in where federal enforcement has been rolled back &#x2014; including the weakening of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau and the Federal Trade Commission &#x2014; and focusing resources on the issues that matter most to working families.

Here at the Oregon DOJ, we&#x2019;re committed to fighting for working families every day. This roundtable was the first step in expanding our knowledge of best practices and increasing collaboration with others.
&#xA0;
Joining us were AG Nick Brown (Washington), AG Keith Ellison (Minnesota), AG Kwame Raoul (Illinois), AG Brian Schwalb (Washington DC), and AG Matthew Platkin (New Jersey).
&#xA0;
