Stay tuned for more town halls in Oregon this summer!","time":"6mo","title":"Oregon Department of Justice"},{"comments_count":2,"date":"2025-06-13T20:25:26.626Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D5622AQGT7KbrzadKAQ/feedshare-shrink_2048_1536/B56ZcaZ9t2HwAo-/0/1748494704497?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=hZDiefNFMZafOew2s2a_Z_ISPR-HrlE4Gj_RUkZ_dOE"],"likes_count":87,"post_id":"7333718336637161472","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/oregon-department-of-justice_today-the-us-court-of-international-trade-activity-7333718336637161472-ktfr","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"Today, the U.S. Court of International Trade struck down the tariffs imposed by President Trump’s executive orders under the International Emergency Economic Powers Act (IEEPA). The decision was made in a multi-state lawsuit led by Oregon Attorney General Dan Rayfield. “The court’s ruling is a victory not just for Oregon, but for working families, small businesses, and everyday Americans. President Trump’s sweeping tariffs were unlawful, reckless, and economically devastating. They triggered retaliatory measures, inflated prices on essential goods, and placed an unfair burden on American families, small businesses and manufacturers. We brought this case because the Constitution doesn’t give any president unchecked authority to upend the economy. This ruling reaffirms that our laws matter, and that trade decisions can’t be made on the president’s whim.” - Attorney General Dan Rayfield","text_html":"Today, the U.S. Court of International Trade struck down the tariffs imposed by President Trump&#x2019;s executive orders under the International Emergency Economic Powers Act (IEEPA). 

The decision was made in a multi-state lawsuit led by Oregon Attorney General Dan Rayfield.

&#x201C;The court&#x2019;s ruling is a victory not just for Oregon, but for working families, small businesses, and everyday Americans. President Trump&#x2019;s sweeping tariffs were unlawful, reckless, and economically devastating. They triggered retaliatory measures, inflated prices on essential goods, and placed an unfair burden on American families, small businesses and manufacturers. We brought this case because the Constitution doesn&#x2019;t give any president unchecked authority to upend the economy. This ruling reaffirms that our laws matter, and that trade decisions can&#x2019;t be made on the president&#x2019;s whim.&#x201D; - Attorney General Dan Rayfield","time":"6mo","title":"Oregon Department of Justice"},{"date":"2025-06-13T20:25:26.629Z","likes_count":62,"post_id":"7331022246318063617","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/oregon-department-of-justice_today-were-in-new-york-for-oral-arguments-activity-7331022246318063617-p8jz","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"Today, we’re in New York for oral arguments for our tariff lawsuit challenging President Trump’s misuse of an emergency power to set tariffs. We’ve heard from unions, small business owners, and more throughout Oregon about the harmful impacts of these tariffs across our state. “President Trump imposed his tariffs without Congress, public input, or restraint — and claims the courts can’t review his decisions. This is a misuse of emergency powers.” - AG Dan Rayfield Read more: https://lnkd.in/enx7kSXh","text_html":"Today, we&#x2019;re in New York for oral arguments for our tariff lawsuit challenging President Trump&#x2019;s misuse of an emergency power to set tariffs. 

We&#x2019;ve heard from unions, small business owners, and more throughout Oregon about the harmful impacts of these tariffs across our state. 

&#x201C;President Trump imposed his tariffs without Congress, public input, or restraint &#x2014; and claims the courts can&#x2019;t review his decisions. This is a misuse of emergency powers.&#x201D; - AG Dan Rayfield 

