&#xA0;&#xA0;
The C&#x2011;suite and business leaders face&#xA0;a clear choice: simplify, compete, innovate&#x2014;or risk falling behind.&#xA0;&#xA0;
&#xA0;&#xA0;
<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fustariffs&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#UStariffs</a> and uncertainty around <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fpillartwo&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#PillarTwo</a> shook confidence. EU simplification is urgent. And Ireland, with its 2026 EU presidency ahead, must lead decisively.&#xA0;&#xA0;
&#xA0;&#xA0;
In this video, we outline why faster interest deductibility&#xA0;reform,&#xA0;and a clearer R&amp;D Compass are essential to sustain Ireland&#x2019;s competitiveness and resilience.&#xA0; 

