&#xA0;
&#x1F335; From red dirt tracks to coastal cliffs and everything in between, we&#x2019;re grateful for the teams who travel these remote corners of Australia every day, making sure communities stay connected no matter how far off the grid the job takes them.","time":"4w","title":"Telstra"},{"comments_count":5,"date":"2025-12-03T13:52:02.875Z","likes_count":240,"post_id":"7401032402371829760","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/telstra_meet-the-good-boy-whose-natural-habitat-is-activity-7401032402371829760-_H44","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"Meet the good boy whose natural habitat is concrete, cables and helping to keep humans out of danger. 🐕👇 🐶 Astro the robot dog explores tunnels and confined areas that are risky for people to enter, gathering environmental data and sending real time insights back to crews above ground. 🦾 Part of a proof of concept developed by Telstra Enterprise and technology partner Ericom , Astro was recently trialled with John Holland on the Metro Tunnel Project in Melbourne. Equipped with sensors, video and IoT connectivity, he can detect gases, assess air quality and share information instantly via Telstra’s 5G network. 👷 This trial shows what advanced connectivity - including private 5G networks and 5G slicing capabilities - can do to support safer, more efficient operations in high risk environments and offers a glimpse of what smarter, more connected worksites could look like.","text_html":"Meet the good boy whose natural habitat is concrete, cables and helping to keep humans out of danger. &#x1F415;&#x1F447;
&#xA0;
&#x1F436; Astro the robot dog explores tunnels and confined areas that are risky for people to enter, gathering environmental data and sending real time insights back to crews above ground.
