lqFG5Pm7XvuZPnG3mizeT_Q02qQE1C_ws"],"likes_count":32,"post_id":"7381908802603913216","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/vect-horus-s-a-s-_eanm2025-nuclearmedicine-vecthorus-activity-7381908802603913216-IMz_","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"🌍 Back from EANM 2025 in Barcelona! Jonathan Nowak and Cédric Malicet had the pleasure of attending the EANM Annual Congress, a key event in the field of nuclear medicine, held this year in Barcelona. It was an inspiring experience filled with cutting-edge science, insightful discussions, and valuable networking. There were several very interesting topics of discussions which are particularly relevant to Vect-Horus: 👉 Advances in radiotheranostics for targeted cancer therapies 👉 Emerging techniques in molecular imaging for neurodegenerative diseases 👉 FAP ligands are clearly in the spotlight and numerous talks and ongoing studies are exploring their potential in both diagnostics and therapy, highlighting the growing interest and momentum around this promising target. These discussions align closely with Vect-Horus’ mission to develop targeted delivery technologies for the brain and tumors and it is exciting to see how the field is evolving. A big thank you to the EANM team for organizing such a rich and forward-looking program! 👉 https://lnkd.in/dwQK3xCT #EANM2025 #NuclearMedicine #VectHorus #Radiotheranostics #MolecularImaging #Biotech #BiotechInnovation #BreakingBarriers","text_html":"&#x1F30D;&#xA0;Back from EANM 2025 in Barcelona! 
&#xA0;
<a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/in/nowakjonathan?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Jonathan Nowak</a> and <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/in/c%C3%A9dric-malicet-163b1617?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>C&#xE9;dric Malicet</a> had the pleasure of attending the&#xA0;EANM Annual Congress, a key event in the field of nuclear medicine, held this year in Barcelona. It was an inspiring experience filled with cutting-edge science, insightful discussions, and valuable networking. 
&#xA0;
There were several very interesting topics of discussions which are particularly relevant to&#xA0;Vect-Horus:
&#xA0;
&#x1F449; Advances in&#xA0;radiotheranostics&#xA0;for targeted cancer therapies 
&#x1F449; Emerging techniques in&#xA0;molecular imaging&#xA0;for neurodegenerative diseases&#xA0; 
&#x1F449; FAP ligands&#xA0;are clearly in the spotlight and numerous talks and ongoing studies are exploring their potential in both diagnostics and therapy, highlighting the growing interest and momentum around this promising target.&#xA0;
&#xA0;
These discussions align closely with Vect-Horus&#x2019; mission to develop targeted delivery technologies for the brain and tumors and it is exciting to see how the field is evolving. A big thank you to the EANM team for organizing such a rich and forward-looking program!
&#xA0;
