d.in/eYq7RhZY","text_html":"Grief is a universal human experience, and for many, it&#x2019;s something they face far earlier in life than they might expect. Yet, it remains a subject too often avoided in conversation. Learning to understand and navigate grief is not just important &#x2014; it&#x2019;s an essential life skill.

The government has now updated its guidance on relationships, sex, and health education, recommending that lessons on coping with bereavement be introduced into school curriculums from September 2026.

This is an encouraging step towards fostering open, compassionate dialogue about loss. My hope is that it will help build deeper understanding, empathy, and emotional resilience in future generations.

