jm8k-E3JWtXtwQ0p006v7xm8ZjGI"],"likes_count":108,"post_id":"7399726049024135168","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/british-arab-commercial-bank_gtrafrica2025-tradefinance-banking-activity-7399726049024135168-sJaZ","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"We were pleased to support Global Trade Review (GTR) ’s Africa London last week, which annually is one of the highlights of the conference calendar. It’s no surprise that trade finance digitalisation is always a core topic at every industry event. Patrick Baatz, CFA , Associate Director, was part of a panel discussion on “MLETR and the Commonwealth Model Law: A status update on adoption in Africa,” exploring the role of banks in trade digitisation and the development of electronic trade frameworks across the continent. As Patrick discussed, the benefits of digitalisation in this sector are clear for both corporates and banks – from a time and cost-savings perspective, but also by making more transactions financeable. Thank you to GTR and all participants for a productive and insightful event. #GTRAfrica2025 #TradeFinance #Banking #Digitalisation #Africa #Partnerships","text_html":"We were pleased to support <a class="link" href="https://uk.linkedin.com/company/exporta?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Global Trade Review (GTR)</a>&#x2019;s Africa London last week, which annually is one of the highlights of the conference calendar.

It&#x2019;s no surprise that trade finance digitalisation is always a core topic at every industry event. <a class="link" href="https://uk.linkedin.com/in/patrick-baatz-cfa-376744148?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Patrick Baatz, CFA</a>, Associate Director, was part of a panel discussion on &#x201C;MLETR and the Commonwealth Model Law: A status update on adoption in Africa,&#x201D; exploring the role of banks in trade digitisation and the development of electronic trade frameworks across the continent.

As Patrick discussed, the benefits of digitalisation in this sector are clear for both corporates and banks &#x2013; from a time and cost-savings perspective, but also by making more transactions financeable. 

Thank you to GTR and all participants for a productive and insightful event.

