Thank you for following us, for engaging with our content, and for being part of this journey.","time":"2w","title":"Egis","videos":["https://dms.licdn.com/playlist/vid/v2/D4E05AQGndoN2h5kc6A/mp4-720p-30fp-crf28/B4EZsmCfsYHECE-/0/1765869761899?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=I167xWmlRJiYZ_GloJm3W7Bo9Zc2qMPFsuw9g5NKFVU","https://dms.licdn.com/playlist/vid/v2/D4E05AQGndoN2h5kc6A/mp4-640p-30fp-crf28/B4EZsmCfsYHEBs-/0/1765869761899?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=bvwEzfqgdJOaYp1hlfDudkB4eGGlrek-otrqN7LuFmM"]},{"comments_count":3,"date":"2025-12-19T14:04:45.874Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E10AQG-sNJO3i8KEw/image-shrink_1280/B4EZsiLdVwGYAM-/0/1765804988498?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=Lk9bD1QrnXwgCDE758cH0G2K9laH0nWbqw2MHp3o1c4"],"likes_count":78,"post_id":"7406322932999954432","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/egis_urban-planning-how-can-trams-and-bikes-coexist-activity-7406322932999954432-cnwp","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"Urban Planning: How Can Trams and Bikes Coexist in Our Cities? 🚋🚲 With cycling up +41% since 2018 and tramway networks expanding across France, ensuring a safe and efficient coexistence between these two modes has become a major urban planning challenge. This position paper highlights key points of friction, particularly at intersections, and proposes practical, operational solutions to better integrate trams and bicycles: traffic flow separation, orthogonal crossings, improved route legibility, and even the adaptation of the Dutch-style intersection (“carrefour hollandais”) to the French context. 👉 Discover the new position paper ‘Cycling vs. Trams: Cohabitation or Confrontation?’ by Florian Bonet , an expert infrastructures, offering timely insights as active mobility continues to grow and tram networks expand. 📄 Dive in to explore analyses, operational recommendations, and real-world case studies. Available for download: - in French: https://lnkd.in/eU252nit - and English: https://lnkd.in/eJ9aGKCS Shirley Hachem","text_html":"Urban Planning: How Can Trams and Bikes Coexist in Our Cities? &#x1F68B;&#x1F6B2;

With cycling up +41% since 2018 and tramway networks expanding across France, ensuring a safe and efficient coexistence between these two modes has become a major urban planning challenge.

This position paper highlights key points of friction, particularly at intersections, and proposes practical, operational solutions to better integrate trams and bicycles: traffic flow separation, orthogonal crossings, improved route legibility, and even the adaptation of the Dutch-style intersection (&#x201C;carrefour hollandais&#x201D;) to the French context.

&#x1F449; Discover the new position paper &#x2018;Cycling vs. Trams: Cohabitation or Confrontation?&#x2019; by <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/in/florianbonet?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Florian Bonet</a>, an expert infrastructures, offering timely insights as active mobility continues to grow and tram networks expand.

&#x1F4C4; Dive in to explore analyses, operational recommendations, and real-world case studies. Available for download: 
- in French: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/eU252nit?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/eU252nit</a>
- and English: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/eJ9aGKCS?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/eJ9aGKCS</a>

<a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/in/shirley-hachem-b34a9548?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Shirley Hachem</a>","time":"2w Edited","title":"Egis"},{"comments_count":1,"date":"2025-12-12T14:04:45.878Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E22AQGpH0KpA09GTg/feedshare-shrink_800/B4EZsSKJeAKMAg-/0/1765536210250?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=qy9rbWXkYzY6NA73OmAvtxR8Gx5bmpN4wAcHKGUE7Wg"],"likes_count":98,"post_id":"7405195592609447936","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/egis_breaking-news-egis-and-its-partners-honoured-activity-7405195592609447936--ivk","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"[Breaking News] 🏆Egis and its partners honoured in the “Public and Landscape spaces” category of the prestigious French prize Equerre d’Argent, for transforming the competition site of Paris 2024 Olympic Games, the Colline d’Elancourt!👏 This iconic project, led by Société de Livraison des Ouvrages Olympiques - SOLIDEO , combines sport, nature, and industrial heritage in the heart of the Île-de-France region in France. 📌Egis, alongside D'ICI LA paysagistes concepteurs (lead contractor), BikeSolutions and l’ ATELIER D'ECOLOGIE URBAINE , oversaw the project management of the site. 💡 Egis is involved in all stages of development for major sports and event projects, from preliminary studies to delivery and commissioning. 👉 The Group is committed to designing high-performance, user-centred and sustainable infrastructure that contributes to the transformation of territories and their social, economic and urban development. More about the project? Read our press release: https://bit.ly/4oS5P0J Egis en France","text_html":"[Breaking News] &#x1F3C6;Egis and its partners honoured in the &#x201C;Public and Landscape spaces&#x201D; category of the prestigious French prize Equerre d&#x2019;Argent, for transforming the competition site of Paris 2024 Olympic Games, the Colline d&#x2019;Elancourt!&#x1F44F; 

This iconic project, led by <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/company/solideofr?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Soci&#xE9;t&#xE9; de Livraison des Ouvrages Olympiques - SOLIDEO</a> , combines sport, nature, and industrial heritage in the heart of the &#xCE;le-de-France region in France. 

&#x1F4CC;Egis, alongside <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/company/d&apos;icilapaysages&amp;territoires?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>D&apos;ICI LA paysagistes concepteurs</a> (lead contractor), <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/company/bikesolutions?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>BikeSolutions</a> and l&#x2019;<a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/company/atelier-d&apos;ecologie-urbaine?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>ATELIER D&apos;ECOLOGIE URBAINE</a>, oversaw the project management of the site. 

&#x1F4A1; <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/company/egis?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Egis</a> is involved in all stages of development for major sports and event projects, from preliminary studies to delivery and commissioning. 

