ur Operations Controllers, who after 40 years, has recently retired from London Luton Airport ✈️ Following 16 years in Security, she then became an Apron Controller for two years. A move to the Ops Control team saw her start overseeing daily operations, a role she's now held for 22 years. Maggie's not just stayed on the ground, she's been in the skies too: “It’s not just the roles that have made my time at London Luton Airport special – it’s the opportunities to do things I never thought I’d do; I’ve flown in a Piper PA aircraft, a helicopter, and once got to go on Concorde – what a thrill! These experiences and my day-to-day roles in such a dynamic environment have made my tenure truly unforgettable. It’s been a privilege to be part of the airport, and I’ve made some fantastic friends for life.” Thank you, Maggie, for your decades of service to the airport 🎊 #LondonLuton #LondonLutonAirport","text_html":"Let&apos;s ceLLAbrate Maggie, one of our Operations Controllers, who after 40 years, has recently retired from London Luton Airport &#x2708;&#xFE0F;

Following 16 years in Security, she then became an Apron Controller for two years. A move to the Ops Control team saw her start overseeing daily operations, a role she&apos;s now held for 22 years.

Maggie&apos;s not just stayed on the ground, she&apos;s been in the skies too: &#x201C;It&#x2019;s not just the roles that have made my time at London Luton Airport special &#x2013; it&#x2019;s the opportunities to do things I never thought I&#x2019;d do; I&#x2019;ve flown in a Piper PA aircraft, a helicopter, and once got to go on Concorde &#x2013; what a thrill! These experiences and my day-to-day roles in such a dynamic environment have made my tenure truly unforgettable. It&#x2019;s been a privilege to be part of the airport, and I&#x2019;ve made some fantastic friends for life.&#x201D;

Thank you, Maggie, for your decades of service to the airport &#x1F38A;

