[{"date":"2025-12-26T13:19:32.669Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E22AQEgU8cPAl-1BQ/feedshare-shrink_1280/B4EZtGppEoGkAw-/0/1766416880389?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=Dtlr9Ox8ggYV1UlHOG9oOqW6ISXdnwGyblfZl31Zsxw"],"likes_count":12,"post_id":"7408889393215823872","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/blglaw_thetariffhomecompanion-tradelaw-internationaltrade-activity-7408889393215823872-Xp7p","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"The conversations that shape Canadian trade policy don't happen in the headlines. They happen in boardrooms, negotiation chambers and policy meetings. The Tariff Home Companion podcast with Rambod Behboodi and Stephen de Boer brings you inside those rooms. The guests aren't just observers. They are the people making the decisions. The first four episodes featured former chief negotiators who drafted the frameworks you work within daily, government officials setting regulatory priorities, and legal experts interpreting the policies before they hit your desk. The mission: shedding light, not heat, on the tariff and trade issues affecting Canada and Canadians. Think of it as your essential year-end listening — perfect for unwinding during the holidays. See full episodes here: https://lnkd.in/efYvkZEa As we look toward 2025, which trade development is keeping you up at night? Is there a guest or topic you’d like us to explore? Let us know in the comments for future episodes. #TheTariffHomeCompanion #TradeLaw #InternationalTrade","text_html":"The conversations that shape Canadian trade policy don&apos;t happen in the headlines. They happen in boardrooms, negotiation chambers and policy meetings. 
&#xA0;
The Tariff Home Companion podcast with <a class="link" href="https://ca.linkedin.com/in/rambodbehboodi?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Rambod Behboodi</a> and <a class="link" href="https://ca.linkedin.com/in/stephen-de-boer-31877832?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Stephen de Boer</a> brings you inside those rooms. The guests aren&apos;t just observers. They are the people making the decisions.
&#xA0;
The first four episodes featured former chief negotiators who drafted the frameworks you work within daily, government officials setting regulatory priorities, and legal experts interpreting the policies before they hit your desk. The mission: shedding light, not heat, on the tariff and trade issues affecting Canada and Canadians.
&#xA0;
Think of it as your essential year-end listening &#x2014; perfect for unwinding during the holidays. See full episodes here: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/efYvkZEa?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/efYvkZEa</a>
&#xA0;
As we look toward 2025, which trade development is keeping you up at night? Is there a guest or topic you&#x2019;d like us to explore? Let us know in the comments for future episodes.
