ll,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"🏆 MODEC Guyana receives GOGEC’s Strategic Local Content & Capacity Builder Award In presenting the award, the Guyana Oil and Gas Energy Chamber highlighted MODEC’s commitment to local talent development through our Offshore Trainee Programme and ongoing efforts to build a highly skilled Guyanese talent pool for Guyana’s energy future. 🚢🌊 🎖️ The recognition was received by Tiffany Hytmiah, HR Coordinator at MODEC in Guyana, and presented by Prime Minister, Hon. Mark Phillips, during GOGEC’s 2025 Annual Awards & Induction Dinner, on November 28th. At the same event, Rafael Fumis , Country Manager at MODEC in Guyana, received a Certificate of Induction, marking MODEC’s membership in the Chamber since January 2025. We are proud to be part of Guyana’s energy journey. 🤝 #bemodec #oilandgas #fpso #development #award #gogec #offshore #guyana","text_html":"&#x1F3C6; MODEC Guyana receives GOGEC&#x2019;s Strategic Local Content &amp; Capacity Builder Award

In presenting the award, the Guyana Oil and Gas Energy Chamber highlighted MODEC&#x2019;s commitment to local talent development through our Offshore Trainee Programme and ongoing efforts to build a highly skilled Guyanese talent pool for Guyana&#x2019;s energy future. &#x1F6A2;&#x1F30A;

&#x1F396;&#xFE0F; The recognition was received by Tiffany Hytmiah, HR Coordinator at MODEC in Guyana, and presented by Prime Minister, Hon. Mark Phillips, during GOGEC&#x2019;s 2025 Annual Awards &amp; Induction Dinner, on November 28th.

At the same event, <a class="link" href="https://gy.linkedin.com/in/rfumis?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Rafael Fumis</a>, Country Manager at MODEC in Guyana, received a Certificate of Induction, marking MODEC&#x2019;s membership in the Chamber since January 2025. 

We are proud to be part of Guyana&#x2019;s energy journey. &#x1F91D;

