sition of its lead investigational asset, efimosfermin alfa, a potential best-in-class therapy in the field of steatotic liver disease. This agreement, under which GSK will pay $1.2 billion upfront, with potential for additional success-based milestone payments totalling $800 million, marks a pivotal moment for Boston Pharmaceuticals and efimosfermin alfa, as both begin a new stage with GSK on a journey with the potential to address a growing global public health concern.

