[{"comments_count":1,"date":"2026-01-01T14:42:48.841Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E10AQH3-Wyux51gvg/image-shrink_1280/B4EZt1J.oxGcAQ-/0/1767197109647?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=NpgrypfBVsi8fS6B9heLWUY6Y7EGYuq8IgyEDSvI-wI"],"likes_count":6,"post_id":"7412161907375120384","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/baystate-health_baystatehealth-activity-7412161907375120384-MBc6","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"As we set intentions for the New Year, prioritizing health is often at the top of the list, and heart health deserves extra attention this time of year. 🎊 The winter months can be a higher-risk time for cardiac events due to increased stress, alcohol and caffeine intake, coupled with large meals, dehydration, cold weather, and disrupted routines. Discovered in 1978 by Dr. Philip Ettinger, Holiday Heart Syndrome (HHS) is a condition in which even otherwise healthy individuals can experience dangerous heart rhythm disturbances, often around major holidays and weekends. 🥂 Recognizing symptoms early and seeking care promptly can be lifesaving. Delaying medical attention just because “it’s the holidays” can lead to serious complications. 🫀 As we look ahead to 2026, visit the #BaystateHealth link in the comments below to learn more on how you can protect yourself and those around you from HHS. 👇","text_html":"As we set intentions for the New Year, prioritizing health is often at the top of the list, and heart health deserves extra attention this time of year. &#x1F38A; 

The winter months can be a higher-risk time for cardiac events due to increased stress, alcohol and caffeine intake, coupled with large meals, dehydration, cold weather, and disrupted routines. 

