ou and your loved ones a season of reflection, rest, and renewed energy for the year ahead! 💙","text_html":"Season&#x2019;s greetings from <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fbaystatehealth&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#BaystateHealth</a> and <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/health-new-england?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Health New England</a>! &#x2744;&#xFE0F; 

This time of year, we reflect on purpose, commitment, and connection. Across cultures and traditions, this season emphasizes gratitude, generosity, and caring for others; values that align deeply with our mission to deliver compassionate, accessible, and high-quality care.&#x2695;&#xFE0F; 

We are grateful for the dedication of our team members and caregivers whose work has supported our communities every day for the last 140 years. 

Wishing you and your loved ones a season of reflection, rest, and renewed energy for the year ahead! &#x1F499; ","time":"1w","title":"Baystate Health"},{"comments_count":1,"date":"2025-12-19T14:42:48.852Z","likes_count":44,"post_id":"7407547375713615872","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/baystate-health_abby-labonte-patient-story-activity-7407547375713615872-lZQP","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"On Valentine's Day, Abby LaBonte, 41, woke up not feeling well, thinking it was the flu. On the way to the hospital, she had a massive heart attack... ❤️🩹 When she arrived at Baystate Medical Center, she was identified as critically ill, in heart failure, and needing to be placed on an Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation (ECMO) Machine. The dedication and persistence of her care team kept her alive while it was determined she would be transferred to Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center for a heart transplant. 🏥 However, with dangerous winter weather conditions at play, Abby was not able to be sent by helicopter. With a perfusionist by her side running the ECMO machine, Abby was transported 90 miles east by ambulance to Boston. 🚑 ❄️ Thanks to the amazing treatment and advocacy from the care team at #BaystateHealth , Abby was kept alive to get to Boston and receive a successful heart transplant. Today, she is alive and grateful. Recently, Abby and her family had the chance to meet the care team that saved her life for the first time! That team was just as grateful to learn how their courage and skill led to such a positive outcome. "It is absolutely incredible...We never get this full-circle moment to see how well people we transport away are doing, so it's kind of emotional." 💬 Take a moment from your day to watch this heartwarming reunion. 💙","text_html":"On Valentine&apos;s Day, Abby LaBonte, 41, woke up not feeling well, thinking it was the flu. On the way to the hospital, she had a massive heart attack... &#x2764;&#xFE0F;&#x1FA79; 

When she arrived at Baystate Medical Center, she was identified as critically ill, in heart failure, and needing to be placed on an Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation (ECMO) Machine. The dedication and persistence of her care team kept her alive while it was determined she would be transferred to <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/beth-israel-deaconess-medical-center?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center</a> for a heart transplant. &#x1F3E5;

However, with dangerous winter weather conditions at play, Abby was not able to be sent by helicopter. With a perfusionist  by her side running the ECMO machine, Abby was transported 90 miles east by ambulance to Boston. &#x1F691; &#x2744;&#xFE0F;

Thanks to the amazing treatment and advocacy from the care team at <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fbaystatehealth&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#BaystateHealth</a>, Abby was kept alive to get to Boston and receive a successful heart transplant. Today, she is alive and grateful. Recently, Abby and her family had the chance to meet the care team that saved her life for the first time!

That team was just as grateful to learn how their courage and skill led to such a positive outcome. 

&quot;It is absolutely incredible...We never get this full-circle moment to see how well people we transport away are doing, so it&apos;s kind of emotional.&quot; &#x1F4AC; 

Take a moment from your day to watch this heartwarming reunion. &#x1F499; ","time":"2w","title":"Baystate Health","videos":["https://dms.licdn.com/playlist/vid/v2/D4E10AQHQbuJlvnkLQw/mp4-720p-30fp-crf28/B4EZszk.J5GoB0-/0/1766096913478?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=gs_2mAt_5X2Gpgkz8Pb3WuMUN8u2YtldMZOqkGa2fB0","https://dms.licdn.com/playlist/vid/v2/D4E10AQHQbuJlvnkLQw/mp4-360p-30fp-crf28/B4EZszk.J5GoBw-/0/1766096903545?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=kPz6ZUWpZlUUoooMPDD_TlAxGm2C0BDviozzBbxSAEM","https://dms.licdn.com/playlist/vid/v2/D4E10AQHQbuJlvnkLQw/mp4-640p-30fp-crf28/B4EZszk.J5GoBU-/0/1766096903545?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=d699f_H0DrxCUJQVHVH4qHBmJ250aVwwqCllhzm8kfo"]},{"comments_count":5,"date":"2025-12-19T14:42:48.853Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E10AQEZS3DFr-_L5g/image-shrink_1280/B4EZsoaJ0QJ0AM-/0/1765909504377?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=AlFFa_aazByxF46wnkCVQMGrtW59wnkktV-gPs500_I"],"likes_count":131,"post_id":"7406761298954457089","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/baystate-health_baystatehealth-activity-7406761298954457089-qZqM","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"Baystate Wing Hospital Named to Forbes ’ Top Hospitals 2026 List! 🏆 We are proud to share that Baystate Wing Hospital has earned national recognition as part of the inaugural Forbes’ Top Hospitals list for 2026. We have received a four-star rating for excellence in clinical outcomes, patient experience, and operational best practices. 🌟 Out of 5,400 acute-care hospitals nationwide, fewer than 15% received a four-star rating or higher, highlighting Baystate Wing’s position among the top-performing hospitals in the U.S. This achievement reflects the dedication of our caregivers and #BaystateHealth ’s unwavering commitment to advancing health, improving outcomes, and delivering compassionate, high-quality care to our Massachusetts communities. 💙","text_html":"Baystate Wing Hospital Named to <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/forbes-magazine?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Forbes</a>&#x2019; Top Hospitals 2026 List! &#x1F3C6; 

We are proud to share that Baystate Wing Hospital has earned national recognition as part of the inaugural Forbes&#x2019; Top Hospitals list for 2026. We have received a four-star rating for excellence in clinical outcomes, patient experience, and operational best practices. &#x1F31F; 

Out of 5,400 acute-care hospitals nationwide, fewer than 15% received a four-star rating or higher, highlighting Baystate Wing&#x2019;s position among the top-performing hospitals in the U.S.

This achievement reflects the dedication of our caregivers and <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fbaystatehealth&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#BaystateHealth</a>&#x2019;s unwavering commitment to advancing health, improving outcomes, and delivering compassionate, high-quality care to our Massachusetts communities. &#x1F499; ","time":"2w","title":"Baystate Health"},{"comments_count":1,"date":"2025-12-19T14:42:48.855Z","likes_count":10,"post_id":"7406390861854425088","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/baystate-health_infocus-featuring-pediatrician-dr-matthew-activity-7406390861854425088-O6i6","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"As cases of Hand, Foot, and Mouth Disease rise rapidly across our region, Baystate Children's Hospital Chair–Department of Pediatrics, Dr. Matthew Di Guglielmo, breaks down what families need to know in WWLP-22News ' InFocus interview. 🎙️ He explains: ▫️ The symptoms, treatment options, and precautions for Hand, Foot, and Mouth Disease. ▫️ How to recognize the differences, and similarities, between this disease and measles. ▫️ Other winter illnesses parents should keep on their radar as we head indoors. Dr. Di Guglielmo also shares insight into his transition to western Massachusetts and his new leadership role. He talks a little about his path into pediatrics, as well as how he communicates with young patients and their families in moments that can feel overwhelming. Whether you're a parent, caregiver, or community member, this conversation offers timely and practical guidance as we navigate a busy respiratory and viral season. 🦠 Watch the full video in the comments below to learn more! ⤵️","text_html":"As cases of Hand, Foot, and Mouth Disease rise rapidly across our region, Baystate Children&apos;s Hospital Chair&#x2013;Department of Pediatrics, Dr. Matthew Di Guglielmo, breaks down what families need to know in <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/22news-wwlp?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>WWLP-22News</a>&apos; InFocus interview. &#x1F399;&#xFE0F; 

He explains:
&#x25AB;&#xFE0F; The symptoms, treatment options, and precautions for Hand, Foot, and Mouth Disease.
&#x25AB;&#xFE0F; How to recognize the differences, and similarities, between this disease and measles.
&#x25AB;&#xFE0F; Other winter illnesses parents should keep on their radar as we head indoors.

Dr. Di Guglielmo also shares insight into his transition to western Massachusetts and his new leadership role. He talks a little about his path into pediatrics, as well as how he communicates with young patients and their families in moments that can feel overwhelming.

Whether you&apos;re a parent, caregiver, or community member, this conversation offers timely and practical guidance as we navigate a busy respiratory and viral season. &#x1F9A0; 

Watch the full video in the comments below to learn more! &#x2935;&#xFE0F; ","time":"2w","title":"Baystate Health"},{"comments_count":1,"date":"2025-12-19T14:42:48.858Z","images":["https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E10AQF9b8XTwPqBkQ/image-shrink_1280/B4EZsUTX6FGYAM-/0/1765572182011?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=Ct4y9GneR6DJP9XtSG9WHattar1G4pYkwcJqyDeTsls"],"likes_count":4,"post_id":"7405346468926205952","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/baystate-health_winter-season-holiday-travel-and-gatherings-activity-7405346468926205952-y4Y5","repost":{"external_links":null,"images":null,"repost_date":null,"repost_followers":null,"repost_hangtags":null,"repost_id":null,"repost_text":null,"repost_title":null,"repost_url":null,"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_users":null,"videos":null},"tagged_companies":null,"tagged_people":null,"text":"As winter arrives in western Massachusetts, so does an increased risk of respiratory illnesses. Infectious disease specialist, Dr. Esteban DelPilar of Baystate Medical Center, spoke with Western Mass News about what our region can expect, how we can protect ourselves and one another. 💙 Dr. DelPilar notes that while it’s too early to predict this season’s severity, indoor gatherings, holiday travel, and close contact continue to drive the spread of viruses like RSV, flu, COVID-19, and the common cold. Earlier this year, Massachusetts saw significant spikes in emergency department visits tied to these illnesses underscoring the importance of prevention. His guidance is clear: 😷 Wear a mask when appropriate, especially while traveling. 🧼 Practice consistent hand hygiene. 💊 Be prepared with basic over-the-counter medications. 🤒 Seek care if symptoms worsen after 48–72 hours. 🧪 Don’t hesitate to get tested for COVID-19 or flu. “We all have the power to protect those who are most vulnerable,” Dr. DelPilar shared — especially as many of us gather, travel, and celebrate throughout the season. ☃️ Read the full story in the comments below! ⤵️","text_html":"As winter arrives in western Massachusetts, so does an increased risk of respiratory illnesses. Infectious disease specialist, Dr. Esteban DelPilar of Baystate Medical Center, spoke with <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/westernmassnews?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Western Mass News</a> about what our region can expect, how we can protect ourselves and one another. &#x1F499; 

Dr. DelPilar notes that while it&#x2019;s too early to predict this season&#x2019;s severity, indoor gatherings, holiday travel, and close contact continue to drive the spread of viruses like RSV, flu, COVID-19, and the common cold. Earlier this year, Massachusetts saw significant spikes in emergency department visits tied to these illnesses underscoring the importance of prevention. 

His guidance is clear:
&#x1F637; Wear a mask when appropriate, especially while traveling.  
&#x1F9FC;  Practice consistent hand hygiene. 
&#x1F48A; Be prepared with basic over-the-counter medications.  
&#x1F912; Seek care if symptoms worsen after 48&#x2013;72 hours. 
&#x1F9EA; Don&#x2019;t hesitate to get tested for COVID-19 or flu.  

&#x201C;We all have the power to protect those who are most vulnerable,&#x201D; Dr. DelPilar shared &#x2014; especially as many of us gather, travel, and celebrate throughout the season. &#x2603;&#xFE0F; 

Read the full story in the comments below! &#x2935;&#xFE0F; ","time":"2w","title":"Baystate Health"}]

